{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"agent_message","text":"The second publish failed because it added a Python float similarity score to the DynamoDB item. The first publish had no related stories, so it stored no score.\n\nI changed the score calculation to use `Decimal` and added a regression test that publishes twice. Both tests pass. The cause, fix, and applicable parts of the colleague’s note are in [ANSWER.md](/tmp/h-bYTJx3/ANSWER.md)."}}
